<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evelyn Baring, 1st Baron Howick of Glendale</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1903">1903</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evelyn Baring, later 1st Baron Howick of Glendale, was a British colonial administrator and governor of Kenya from 1952 to 1959. Soon after arriving he declared a state of emergency against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mau-mau-rebellion">Mau Mau uprising</a>, which led to mass detention of Kikuyu and the hanging of more than a thousand rebels. He earlier served as governor of Southern Rhodesia and high commissioner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evelyn-baring-1st-baron-howick-of-glendale.jpg" alt="Evelyn Baring, 1st Baron Howick of Glendale" width="320" height="587" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ottoline Morrell (1873–1938) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evelyn_Baring,_I_baron_Howick_of_Glendale1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
